<title>GERMANY: Bonn sells 8.51 bln dmk series 121 Bobls.</title>
<headline>Bonn sells 8.51 bln dmk series 121 Bobls.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German government sold 8.51 billion marks ($5.1 billion) of its Series 121 five-year 4.75 percent Bundesobligation, known as &quot;Bobls,&quot; at 101.43 and above, the Bundesbank said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The Bundesbank, which is the issuing agent, said it would retain 997 million marks of the debt. The size of the tap tranche, sales to individuals, was put at 2.49 billion marks, making the total Series 121 issue volume 12 billion marks.</p>
<p>The average yield on the sale was 4.38 percent.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom + 49 69 756525 ($ = 1.677 German Marks)</p>
